    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a public company founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, California, traded on the Nasdaq under the ticker WDAY. It offers cloud-based software for human resources, finance, and IT, and its most recently reported annual revenue was $9,552,000,000 for the period ending January 31, 2026. The company describes itself as an enterprise AI platform and positions its software as covering core business processes across those three domains.\n\nWorkday's primary AI product, listed as Workday AI, is described on the company's site as enabling teams of specialized agents to perform key processes across HR, finance, and IT. The site references agentic AI capabilities alongside a product or integration called Sana, describing agents that can find, build, act, and automate rather than simply assist. The held facts note that the product touches sensitive HR data and incorporates skills-based talent management and predictive analytics.\n\nThe site's held facts record nine federal civil cases filed against Workday across multiple district courts, including the Eastern District of California, the Northern District of Georgia, the Northern District of California, the District of Colorado, the District of Maryland, and the Eastern District of Virginia. The cases include matters under the names Meckfessel Poletti v. Workday, Inc., Williams v. Workday, Inc., Elias v. Workday, Inc., Noriega v. Workday, Inc., Hill v. Workday, Inc., and Doe v. Workday, Inc. No MCP server registration is on record for the company.",
